This project is a fork of:

    Chatbot with RAG and LangChain
    https://github.com/ThomasJanssen-tech/Chatbot-with-RAG-and-LangChain
    Copyright (c) 2025 Thomas Janssen
    MIT License

The structure (a separate ingest step writing to a persistent Chroma store, and
a query step reading from it) is taken from that project. The MIT licence of the
original is reproduced in LICENSE alongside this fork's own grant.

What is NOT carried over, and why, is set out in README under "What changed from
the reference". In short: content-addressed chunk ids, surviving citations, a
measured abstention threshold, a question set with unanswerable questions in it,
and no language model in the retrieval path.

The reference repository also contains, at data/NIPS-2017-attention-is-all-you-
need-Paper.pdf, the NIPS 2017 paper by Vaswani et al. A repository-wide MIT
grant does not extend to a third party's published paper, so no corpus is
committed here at all. See README, section "The corpus".
